66744; --pix-note-grid-header-bg: #1a1a1a\\\"><thead><tr><th>MODEL</th><th>DISTILL</th><th>STEPS</th><th>CFG</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Base</td><td>N</td><td>50+</td><td>7+</td></tr><tr><td>Not Base</td><td>Y</td><td>8+</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-dashed\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span>Default sampler: LCM</span></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span>Default Scheduler: Simple</span></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-dashed\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><h1>Place in: models/checkpoints</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><a href=\\\"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/stable-audio-3/resolve/main/checkpoints/stable_audio_3_medium.safetensors?download=true\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">stable_audio_3_medium.safetensors</a></h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><br></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><h1>Place in: models/text_encoders</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><a href=\\\"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/stable-audio-3/resolve/main/text_encoders/t5gemma_b_b_ul2.safetensors?download=true\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">t5gemma_b_b_ul2.safetensors</a></h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><br></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Workflow Assembly: <span>Marco Capelli</span><br><span>X:</span>&nbsp;<a href=\\\"https://x.com/adamdived1\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">https://x.com/adamdived1</a></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-dashed\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><h2>Prompt structure:</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>According to Stable Audio's official prompt structure guide, the order of elements matters, starting with Format and Genre and layering in instruments, mood, and BPM consistently yields better results. Setting Format: Band signals a full instrumental track rather than a single stem.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><br></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Format: Band | Genre: Rock | Subgenre: Easy Rock, Commercial Pop-Rock | Instruments: bright electric guitars with light chorus, punchy snare drum kit, driving bass guitar, uplifting piano stabs, subtle synth pad | Mood: Upbeat, Energizing, Optimistic, Feel-Good, Driving | Style: 2020s, Advertising, Film Instrumental | BPM: 120</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><br></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Format: Electronic | Genre: Techno | Subgenre: Detroit Techno, Dark Techno, Industrial | Instruments: pounding 909 kick drum, distorted acid bassline, cold metallic hi-hats, eerie pitch-shifted synth pads, hypnotic looping arpeggiator, industrial noise textures, gated reverb snare | Mood: Dark, Hypnotic, Relentless, Cold, Dystopian, Trance-Inducing | Style: 1990s Detroit Underground, Warehouse Club, Industrial Electronics | BPM: 135</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><br></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Format: Band | Genre: Rock | Subgenre: Dark Rock, Psychedelic Rock, Occult Rock | Instruments: heavily reverbed distorted electric guitar with wah-wah and tremolo, droning fuzz bass, slow pounding live drum kit with tribal feel, haunting organ swells, eerie theremin-like synth lead, layered feedback textures, ritualistic percussion | Mood: Hypnotic, Hallucinogenic, Dark, Ritualistic, Unsettling, Trance-Inducing, Oppressive | Style: 1970s Psychedelic Underground, Desert Rock, Occult Doom, Stoner Rock | BPM: 70</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-dashed\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2>Instruments STEM structure:</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p><br></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>For DRUMS only stem example:</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Strip out all melodic and harmonic instruments and focus the entire prompt on the drum kit.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><br></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>positive prompt:</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Format: Drum Stem | Genre: Synthwave, Retrowave | Subgenre: Electro, Outrun | Instruments: electronic drum machine, LinnDrum, TR-808 kick drum, gated reverb snare, punchy rimshot, tight closed hi-hats, open hi-hat, claps, electronic tom fills, sidechained kick transients | Mood: Driving, Punchy, Mechanical, Energetic | Style: 1980s Drum Machine, Electronic Percussion, Giorgio Moroder, Miami Vice | BPM: 110</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><br></p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>negative prompt:<br>synth, bass, chords, pads, melody, strings, piano, arpeggio, guitar, harmony, lead, atmosphere, reverb tails, ambient</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"width\":480.2419553063437,\"height\":511.6199306306503,\"backgroundColor\":\"#000000\"}",""],"color":"#000000","bgcolor":"#000000"}],"links":[[2,1,2,5,0,"VAE"],[3,2,0,6,0,"CLIP"],[4,1,0,7,0,"MODEL"],[5,7,0,8,0,"MODEL"],[6,8,0,9,0,"*"],[7,17,0,16,0,"CLIP"],[13,37,0,36,0,"MODEL"],[18,46,0,36,1,"CONDITIONING"],[19,47,0,36,2,"CONDITIONING"],[26,36,0,54,0,"LATENT"],[27,53,0,54,1,"VAE"],[33,62,0,61,0,"CLIP"],[35,51,0,36,3,"LATENT"],[38,54,0,69,0,"AUDIO"],[43,54,0,79,0,"AUDIO"],[50,61,0,45,0,"CONDITIONING"],[51,16,0,35,0,"CONDITIONING"]],"groups":[{"id":1,"title":"Load Models","bounding":[-6736.152066601443,2458.641799925449,1239.818450131128,375.87163367335825],"color":"#b58b2a","flags":{}},{"id":2,"title":"Drum Stem Prompts","bounding":[-6736.202585194875,2857.0879943705154,1037.2851975170151,531.3835787600738],"color":"#1f85a8","flags":{}},{"id":3,"title":"Sampler","bounding":[-5676.202383020366,2857.0865077441713,1180.6132877963482,613.0972093366227],"color":"#8A8","flags":{}}],"config":{},"extra":{"ue_links":[],"ds":{"scale":1.305927329411901,"offset":[7320.408314930023,-3403.047487689452]},"links_added_by_ue":[]},"version":0.4}